      "dom_id": "question-46426",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "If $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are polynomials of degree $3$ and $5$, respectively, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P+Q$ is always a polynomial\n\nII. $P\\cdot Q$ is always a polynomial\n\nIII. $\\frac{P}{Q}$ is always a polynomial",
      "worked_solution": "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Polynomials are closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. Polynomials are closed under multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, suppose $P={x}^{3}$ and $Q={x}^{5}.$ Then $\\frac{P}{Q}=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{5}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},$ which is not a polynomial.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and II are true.",
