      "dom_id": "question-51691",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given that $P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $5,$ which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $P(x)-4{x}^{6}$ is a polynomial\n\nII. $4{x}^{6}\\cdot P(x)$ is a polynomial\n\nIII. $\\frac{4{x}^{6}}{P(x)}$ is a polynomial",
      "worked_solution": "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Polynomials are closed under subtraction.\n\n- Statement II is true. Polynomials are closed under multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, suppose $P(x)={x}^{5}+1.$ Then $\\frac{4{x}^{6}}{P(x)}=\\frac{4{x}^{6}}{{x}^{5}+1},$ which is not a polynomial.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and II are true.",
