      "dom_id": "question-111383",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "If $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are polynomials of degree $5$, what is the highest possible degree of $P+Q?$",
      "worked_solution": "The highest possible degree of $P+Q$ is $5.$\n\nFor example, suppose $P={x}^{5}$ and $Q={x}^{5}.$ Then $P+Q=2{x}^{5}.$ \n\nSince neither $P$ nor $Q$ contain terms of order higher than ${x}^{5},$ $P+Q$ can't contain terms of order higher than ${x}^{5}.$",
